window.EDPM_LABS = (window.EDPM_LABS || []).concat([{"id":"S1-L1","sec":"S1","units":["S1U1","S1U2","S1U3"],"app":"windows","level":"Foundation","title":"Inside your computer: specs, storage and devices","time":60,"brief":"<p>Find out what is inside the computer you use at school, then map its devices to the IPOS cycle.</p>","data":"<h4>Recording sheet</h4><table><tr><th>Item</th><th>Where to find it</th><th>Your value</th></tr><tr><td>Processor name, cores, GHz</td><td>Settings ▸ System ▸ About; Task Manager ▸ Performance ▸ CPU</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Installed RAM</td><td>Settings ▸ System ▸ About</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Storage type and capacity, free space</td><td>File Explorer ▸ This PC; Task Manager ▸ Disk</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Operating system and version</td><td>Settings ▸ System ▸ About</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Screen resolution</td><td>Settings ▸ System ▸ Display</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Ports on the outside of the computer</td><td>Look (do not open the case)</td><td></td></tr></table>","tasks":["Open the Windows Desktop Lab (or a real school PC) and complete the recording sheet.","Convert the RAM and total storage into MB using 1 GB = 1,024 MB; show working.","List every input, output and storage device connected to the computer and sort them into an IPOS table.","Identify whether the main drive is an HDD or SSD and give one advantage of that type.","Calculate how many 5 MB photos would fit in the free space."],"skills":["Reading system specifications","Storage unit conversion","Classifying devices by IPOS","Comparing HDD and SSD"],"check":[{"c":"Recording sheet complete and accurate","m":4},{"c":"Conversions correct with working","m":3},{"c":"IPOS device table correct","m":4},{"c":"Drive type identified with advantage","m":2},{"c":"Photo calculation correct","m":2}],"tip":"Never open the computer case to look for parts; every value you need is in Settings, Task Manager or File Explorer."},{"id":"S1-L2","sec":"S1","units":["S1U4","S1U5"],"app":"windows","level":"Core","title":"System software and troubleshooting toolkit","time":75,"brief":"<p>Use operating-system tools and utilities to manage files, monitor performance and diagnose common faults, the way a help-desk technician would.</p>","data":"<h4>Scenario cards</h4><ol><li>A browser is 'Not responding'.</li><li>The PC is slow; memory is at 95%.</li><li>A laptop has no Internet, but the phone on the same Wi-Fi works.</li><li>The disk is almost full.</li><li>A student cannot find her SBA folder.</li></ol>","tasks":["Create the folder structure SBA ▸ Word, Excel, Access; create, rename, move and delete a test file. Name the OS function you used each time.","Open Task Manager (Ctrl+Shift+Esc); record CPU, memory and disk use; end a 'not responding' task in the simulator.","Turn airplane mode on and off; run ipconfig and ping in Command Prompt; explain what each output tells you.","Use Disk Cleanup (or the simulator's equivalent) and Windows Security to scan; explain what each utility does.","For each scenario card, write the steps you would take, in order, with a reason for each.","Classify every program you used as OS, utility or application software."],"skills":["File management","Using Task Manager","Command line basics (ipconfig, ping)","Utilities","Systematic troubleshooting"],"check":[{"c":"Folder tasks completed with OS functions named","m":3},{"c":"Task Manager readings recorded and task ended","m":3},{"c":"ipconfig/ping run and explained","m":3},{"c":"Utilities used and explained","m":2},{"c":"Five scenarios solved logically with reasons","m":5},{"c":"Software correctly classified","m":2}],"tip":"Change one thing at a time and test after each change, so you know exactly what fixed the problem."},{"id":"S1-L3","sec":"S1","units":["S1U6","S1U7"],"app":"access","level":"Challenge","title":"Validated data capture for a credit union","time":90,"brief":"<p>Build a membership table and form for the Leeward Credit Union with full validation, then test it with normal, boundary and erroneous data.</p>","data":"<h4>Field specification</h4><table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Rule</th></tr><tr><td>MemberID</td><td>Short Text (6)</td><td>Two letters then four digits, e.g. LC1234 (input mask LL0000)</td></tr><tr><td>Surname</td><td>Short Text</td><td>Required</td></tr><tr><td>DateOfBirth</td><td>Date/Time</td><td>Member must be born on or before 31/12/2010</td></tr><tr><td>MonthlySavings</td><td>Currency</td><td>Between 10 and 2000</td></tr><tr><td>Phone</td><td>Short Text (7)</td><td>Exactly 7 digits</td></tr><tr><td>JoinDate</td><td>Date/Time</td><td>Not later than today</td></tr></table><h4>Test data</h4><table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Normal</th><th>Boundary</th><th>Erroneous</th></tr><tr><td>MonthlySavings</td><td>350</td><td>10 and 2000</td><td>9, 2001, 'abc'</td></tr><tr><td>MemberID</td><td>LC2045</td><td>AA0000</td><td>LC20, 1234LC</td></tr></table>","tasks":["Create the table in Design View with the data types and field sizes given.","Set validation rules and validation text: Between 10 And 2000 for MonthlySavings; <=#31/12/2010# for DateOfBirth; <=Date() for JoinDate; Required = Yes for Surname.","Add an input mask LL0000 for MemberID and 0000000 for Phone (length/format checks).","Create a form for data entry; enter five valid members.","Test every rule with the normal, boundary and erroneous data; record the result in a test table with screenshots of the error messages.","Calculate the check digit for MemberID numbers 2045 and 3142 (weights 5, 4, 3, 2, modulus 11) and explain how it would catch a transposition.","Write a paragraph recommending a file organisation for the member file and explaining which errors validation cannot catch and how verification helps."],"skills":["Table design","Validation rules and text","Input masks","Testing with normal, boundary and erroneous data","Check digits","Choosing file organisation"],"check":[{"c":"Table design correct","m":3},{"c":"All validation rules and masks working","m":6},{"c":"Test table complete with evidence","m":5},{"c":"Check digits correct","m":2},{"c":"Recommendation paragraph sound","m":4}],"tip":"Boundary values (exactly 10 and exactly 2000) should be ACCEPTED; values just outside (9 and 2001) should be REJECTED. If not, check whether you used < or <=."},{"id":"S2-L1","sec":"S2","units":["S2U1","S2U2","S2U4"],"app":"windows","level":"Foundation","title":"Explore your connection: ipconfig, ping and nslookup","time":45,"brief":"<p>Use command-line tools to see your computer's place in the network: its IP address, MAC address, default gateway (router) and how it reaches websites. Use the Windows Desktop Lab or a school PC.</p>","data":"<h4>Commands you will use</h4><table><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it shows</th></tr><tr><td><code>ipconfig</code></td><td>IP address, subnet mask, default gateway</td></tr><tr><td><code>ipconfig /all</code></td><td>Also the physical (MAC) address and DNS servers</td></tr><tr><td><code>ping 8.8.8.8</code></td><td>Whether you can reach a server on the Internet, and the round-trip time in ms</td></tr><tr><td><code>ping www.example.com</code></td><td>The same, by name (tests DNS too)</td></tr><tr><td><code>nslookup www.example.com</code></td><td>The IP address DNS returns for a name</td></tr><tr><td><code>tracert www.example.com</code></td><td>Each router (hop) between you and the site</td></tr></table>","tasks":["Open Command Prompt (Windows Desktop Lab ▸ Command Prompt).","Run ipconfig. Record your IPv4 address and default gateway. Explain in one sentence what the default gateway is.","Run ipconfig /all. Record your physical (MAC) address and say which device it belongs to (NIC).","Open Settings ▸ Network & Internet ▸ Wi-Fi and record the security type (e.g. WPA2/WPA3). Say why it matters.","Run ping 8.8.8.8 and record the average time. Then run ping www.example.com and record the IP address shown.","Run nslookup www.example.com. Explain which system (DNS) produced the answer and why it is needed.","Run tracert www.example.com (or view the simulated output). Count the hops and say which device type each hop is.","Write a 5-line summary: 'How my computer reaches a website'."],"skills":["Using the command line","Reading IP and MAC addresses","Testing connectivity","Explaining DNS and routers"],"check":[{"c":"IPv4 address and default gateway recorded and explained","m":2},{"c":"MAC address recorded and linked to the NIC","m":2},{"c":"Wi-Fi security type recorded with reason","m":1},{"c":"Ping results recorded and interpreted","m":2},{"c":"nslookup result and DNS explained","m":2},{"c":"Clear summary of the path to a website","m":3}],"tip":"If ping by name fails but ping 8.8.8.8 works, the Internet connection is fine and DNS is the problem: a classic troubleshooting clue."},{"id":"S2-L2","sec":"S2","units":["S2U1","S2U2"],"app":"diagram","level":"Core","title":"Design the Castle Bruce Community Centre network","time":60,"brief":"<p>The <b>Castle Bruce Community Centre</b> has received 12 desktops and a printer. It wants a computer lab, guest Wi-Fi for visitors, a link to a second building 250 m away and Internet access. Design the network using a diagramming tool (draw.io, Visio, PowerPoint shapes or paper).</p>","data":"<h4>Site facts</h4><table><tr><th>Item</th><th>Detail</th></tr><tr><td>Lab</td><td>12 desktops, 1 network printer, cable runs 15–40 m to the comms cupboard</td></tr><tr><td>Visitors</td><td>Up to 30 phones/tablets in the hall</td></tr><tr><td>Second building</td><td>250 m away across a car park; 3 laptops and a printer</td></tr><tr><td>ISP</td><td>Fibre to the main building (ONT supplied)</td></tr><tr><td>Environment</td><td>Frequent lightning in rainy season; occasional power cuts</td></tr></table><h4>Illustrative price list</h4><table><tr><th>Item</th><th>Price (EC$)</th></tr><tr><td>24-port switch</td><td>180</td></tr><tr><td>8-port switch</td><td>45</td></tr><tr><td>Router with firewall</td><td>150</td></tr><tr><td>Wireless access point</td><td>110</td></tr><tr><td>Cat6 cable (per 100 m)</td><td>60</td></tr><tr><td>Fibre link 250 m (installed)</td><td>1,200</td></tr><tr><td>Point-to-point wireless bridge (pair)</td><td>400</td></tr><tr><td>UPS</td><td>130</td></tr></table>","tasks":["Draw the network diagram for both buildings using a star topology in each, labelling every device and link.","Label each link with its medium (Cat6, fibre or wireless) and state why.","Choose between fibre and a wireless bridge for the 250 m link. Write a justification that weighs cost, weather and security.","Show a separate guest WLAN and explain how it protects the lab computers.","Write a function statement for each device type in your design.","Produce a cost table using the illustrative prices and total it.","Add two resilience measures for hurricane season and explain them."],"skills":["Network design","Choosing components and media","Justifying decisions","Costing"],"check":[{"c":"Accurate, labelled diagram of both buildings","m":4},{"c":"Media chosen and labelled with reasons","m":3},{"c":"250 m link choice justified (cost, weather, security)","m":3},{"c":"Guest WLAN separation explained","m":2},{"c":"Device functions correct","m":3},{"c":"Cost table accurate","m":2},{"c":"Two resilience measures","m":2}],"tip":"Twisted pair is limited to about 100 m per run. Anything longer needs fibre, a wireless bridge, or a switch part-way."},{"id":"S2-L3","sec":"S2","units":["S2U3","S2U2"],"app":"excel","level":"Core","title":"Which mobile plan? Data, bandwidth and cost","time":50,"brief":"<p>Your cousin is starting Form 4 and needs a mobile plan for online classes, WhatsApp, streaming and hotspotting a laptop for SBA work. Compare three plans in a spreadsheet and recommend one.</p>","data":"<h4>Sample plans (illustrative)</h4><table><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Monthly cost (US$)</th><th>Data (GB)</th><th>Speed (Mbps)</th><th>Hotspot allowed?</th><th>Regional roaming</th></tr><tr><td>Island Lite</td><td>15</td><td>5</td><td>20</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Island Plus</td><td>30</td><td>20</td><td>50</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Island Max 5G</td><td>50</td><td>60</td><td>200</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr></table><h4>Typical monthly use (estimate)</h4><table><tr><th>Activity</th><th>Data</th></tr><tr><td>Teams/Classroom video lessons, 10 hours</td><td>about 5 GB</td></tr><tr><td>WhatsApp messages and calls</td><td>about 2 GB</td></tr><tr><td>Streaming video, 8 hours</td><td>about 6 GB</td></tr><tr><td>Hotspot for SBA uploads/downloads</td><td>about 3 GB</td></tr></table>","tasks":["Enter the plans into a spreadsheet. Add a column for cost per GB using a formula (=Cost/Data) and format it as currency.","Calculate the cousin's total monthly data use with SUM.","Use IF to show 'Enough' or 'Not enough' for each plan's data allowance.","Calculate how long a 750 MB video would take to download on each plan's speed (=750*8/Speed) in seconds.","Create a column chart comparing cost per GB.","Write a recommendation (100–150 words) that considers data, speed, hotspot, cost and roaming, and mentions one security habit for mobile use."],"skills":["Spreadsheet formulas (SUM, IF, division)","Bandwidth calculations","Charting","Evaluating options"],"check":[{"c":"Correct cost-per-GB formulas","m":2},{"c":"Correct total data with SUM","m":1},{"c":"Working IF formulas","m":2},{"c":"Correct download-time formulas","m":2},{"c":"Suitable labelled chart","m":2},{"c":"Justified recommendation with a security habit","m":3}],"tip":"Remember the ×8: speeds are in megabits per second, but file sizes are in megabytes."},{"id":"S2-L4","sec":"S2","units":["S2U4"],"app":"web","level":"Challenge","title":"Publish and dissect a website","time":75,"brief":"<p>Build a small site for <b>Coral Reef Café</b> in the Web Page Builder, publish it via FTP, and then analyse how the Web delivers it, from URL to padlock.</p>","data":"<h4>Content for the café</h4><table><tr><th>Page</th><th>Content</th></tr><tr><td>index.html (Home)</td><td>Logo text 'Coral Reef Café', welcome paragraph, photo of johnny cakes (alt text), navigation</td></tr><tr><td>menu.html</td><td>Table: Johnny cakes $4, Saltfish $9, Mango smoothie $6, Fish &amp; fungi $14; bookmark section 'Drinks'</td></tr><tr><td>contact.html</td><td>Address: Frigate Bay; e-mail link; link to a downloadable PDF menu</td></tr></table><h4>Example URL</h4><p><code>https://www.coralreefcafe.kn/menu.html#drinks</code></p>","tasks":["Build the three pages with consistent navigation on each page.","Include all four hyperlink types: another page, a bookmark (#drinks), an e-mail address (mailto:) and a file (the PDF menu).","View the HTML code for one page and identify the tags for a heading, paragraph, image (with alt text) and hyperlink.","Publish the site with the FTP step. Write down the server address field, the direction of transfer (upload) and why SFTP is safer than plain FTP.","Label every part of the example URL (protocol, subdomain, domain name, TLD, file name, fragment).","Explain in 6 numbered steps how a visitor's browser loads menu.html, mentioning DNS, IP address, HTTPS request and rendering.","Evaluate your site on accuracy, navigation, display on a phone and load time, and suggest two improvements."],"skills":["Web page creation","Hyperlinks","Reading HTML","Publishing via FTP","Explaining DNS/HTTP(S)","Website evaluation"],"check":[{"c":"Three linked pages with consistent navigation","m":3},{"c":"All four hyperlink types working","m":4},{"c":"HTML tags correctly identified","m":2},{"c":"Published with correct upload/FTP explanation","m":2},{"c":"URL fully labelled","m":2},{"c":"Accurate 6-step loading sequence","m":3},{"c":"Evaluation with two improvements","m":2}],"tip":"A bookmark link only works if the target element has a matching id, e.g. an element with id=\"drinks\" for #drinks."},{"id":"S3-L1","sec":"S3","units":["S3U1","S3U3"],"app":"windows","level":"Foundation","title":"Security check-up in Windows","time":50,"brief":"<p>You are the new student IT assistant at the Pietermaai Youth Centre. Check the security of a Windows PC and record what you find, using the Windows Desktop Lab or a real school PC.</p>","data":"<h4>Security check-up record</h4><table><tr><th>Item</th><th>Where to find it</th><th>Status</th><th>Action needed?</th></tr><tr><td>Virus and threat protection</td><td>Windows Security</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Firewall and network protection</td><td>Windows Security</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Windows Update</td><td>Settings ▸ Windows Update</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Screen lock / sign-in options</td><td>Settings ▸ Accounts</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Backup</td><td>Settings / OneDrive</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>User account type</td><td>Settings ▸ Accounts</td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>","tasks":["Open Windows Security and record the status of virus and threat protection and the firewall.","Run a quick virus scan and record the result.","Check for Windows updates and note the date of the last update.","Check the sign-in options and whether the account is a standard user or administrator.","Find out whether files are backed up (e.g. OneDrive) and record it.","Write three recommendations for the youth centre, each linked to a threat from Unit 1."],"skills":["Navigating Windows Security and Settings","Running a virus scan","Checking updates","Linking countermeasures to threats"],"check":[{"c":"All six items recorded accurately","m":6},{"c":"Quick scan run and result recorded","m":2},{"c":"Three recommendations linked to specific threats","m":6}],"tip":"A standard user account for everyday use is safer than an administrator account: malware runs with the permissions of the logged-in user."},{"id":"S3-L2","sec":"S3","units":["S3U2","S3U4"],"app":"research","level":"Core","title":"Caribbean IT jobs market research","time":70,"brief":"<p>Research current IT job adverts in the Caribbean (company websites, newspapers such as The Valley Courier, job boards) and build a short report on the skills employers want and how automation is changing work.</p>","data":"<h4>Job advert record</h4><table><tr><th>Job title</th><th>Employer type</th><th>Country</th><th>Main duties</th><th>Qualifications/certifications</th><th>Remote possible?</th></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table><h4>Sources checklist</h4><ul><li>Author/organisation named?</li><li>Date of the advert?</li><li>Genuine company (website, contact details)?</li></ul>","tasks":["Find and record at least FIVE genuine IT job adverts from at least two Caribbean countries.","Classify each advert by the professional roles in Unit 4.","Summarise in a spreadsheet the most frequently requested skills and certifications.","Identify one job that exists because of new technology and one that is threatened by automation.","Write a 300-word conclusion: what should a Form 5 student do now to prepare?"],"skills":["Evaluating online sources","Classifying job roles","Summarising data in a spreadsheet","Writing a conclusion from evidence"],"check":[{"c":"Five adverts recorded with all fields","m":5},{"c":"Roles correctly classified","m":4},{"c":"Skills summary table or chart","m":3},{"c":"Automation analysis","m":3},{"c":"Evidence-based conclusion","m":5}],"tip":"Never pay to apply for a job. A genuine employer will not ask for money; treat any such advert as a scam and note it as an example."},{"id":"S3-L3","sec":"S3","units":["S3U3","S3U5"],"app":"word","level":"Challenge","title":"Security and ICT plan for a small business","time":90,"brief":"<p>Montego Bay Dive & Tours (8 staff) wants to modernise: online bookings, EPOS in its gift shop, cloud storage and drone filming for marketing. Write a professional ICT and security plan for the owner.</p>","data":"<h4>Business profile</h4><table><tr><th>Item</th><th>Current situation</th></tr><tr><td>Computers</td><td>3 PCs on the ground floor near the beach; 1 shared admin password</td></tr><tr><td>Data</td><td>Customer names, medical forms, card details on one PC</td></tr><tr><td>Backups</td><td>USB stick in the office drawer</td></tr><tr><td>Network</td><td>Open Wi-Fi shared with customers</td></tr><tr><td>Budget</td><td>US$5,000 this year</td></tr><tr><td>Plans</td><td>Online booking, EPOS gift shop, cloud storage, drone filming</td></tr></table>","tasks":["Create a professional document with a title page, heading styles and a table of contents.","Identify at least SIX vulnerabilities and the threats that could exploit them (table).","Recommend physical, software and personal/policy countermeasures for each, with estimated costs within budget.","Explain the benefits and drawbacks of the planned EPOS, online booking, cloud and drone technologies for the business.","Include a one-page acceptable use policy for staff.","Finish with a prioritised action plan for the first three months."],"skills":["Professional document formatting","Risk analysis tables","Recommending and costing countermeasures","Evaluating ICT for a business","Writing policy"],"check":[{"c":"Professional formatting with TOC and styles","m":4},{"c":"Six vulnerabilities with matching threats","m":6},{"c":"Layered, costed countermeasures within budget","m":8},{"c":"Balanced evaluation of the four technologies","m":6},{"c":"AUP and prioritised action plan","m":6}],"tip":"Start with free measures (individual accounts, updates, MFA, built-in antivirus, Wi-Fi password) and spend the budget where risk is highest: off-site backup, a UPS and a secure payment provider."},{"id":"S4-L1","sec":"S4","units":["S4U1","S4U2"],"app":"word","level":"Foundation","title":"The Beach Clean-Up report","time":60,"brief":"<p>Format and edit a two-page report for <b>San Fernando Beach Clean-Up Project</b>, using content from several sources.</p>","data":"<h4>Content to use</h4><table><tr><th>Item</th><th>Source</th></tr><tr><td>Report text (about 400 words)</td><td>Typed from your teacher's handout</td></tr><tr><td>Volunteer quote</td><td>A paragraph copied from the club's web page</td></tr><tr><td>Rubbish collected</td><td>January 42 kg, February 37 kg, March 51 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Photo</td><td>cleanup.jpg (provided)</td></tr></table>","tasks":["Type the report text and paste the volunteer quote using Keep Text Only, in quotation marks, with a footnote citing the source.","Apply Title, Heading 1 and Normal styles; set line spacing to 1.15 and 6 pt after paragraphs.","Insert the photo with Square text wrapping and a caption.","Insert a three-row table of rubbish collected with a shaded header row; right-align the numbers.","Insert a header with the project name and a footer with automatic page numbers.","Use Find and Replace to change every “beach cleanup” to “beach clean-up”.","Run a spelling and grammar check, proofread, and check the word count is under 600 words."],"skills":["Paste options","Styles","Text wrapping","Tables","Headers and footers","Footnotes","Find and Replace","Proofing"],"check":[{"c":"Quote pasted as plain text and footnoted","m":2},{"c":"Styles applied to title and headings","m":2},{"c":"Photo wrapped and captioned","m":2},{"c":"Table correct and formatted","m":2},{"c":"Header, footer and page numbers","m":2},{"c":"All replacements made, no spelling errors","m":2}],"tip":"Turn on Show/Hide ¶ before you start: you will spot stray Enter presses and spaces immediately."},{"id":"S4-L2","sec":"S4","units":["S4U2","S4U3"],"app":"word","level":"Core","title":"Sports Camp letters, labels and registration form","time":90,"brief":"<p>Produce the mail merge and form for <b>Trinidad and Tobago Youth Sports Camp</b>.</p>","data":"<h4>Data source (Campers.xlsx)</h4><table><tr><th>Title</th><th>ParentFirstName</th><th>ParentLastName</th><th>CamperName</th><th>AgeGroup</th><th>Sport</th><th>Balance</th></tr><tr><td>Ms.</td><td>Shanice</td><td>Hodge</td><td>Jaden</td><td>U13</td><td>Football</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Mr.</td><td>Ravi</td><td>Mahabir</td><td>Asha</td><td>U15</td><td>Cricket</td><td>85</td></tr><tr><td>Mrs.</td><td>Ana</td><td>Rodriguez</td><td>Luis</td><td>U13</td><td>Swimming</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Dr.</td><td>Kwame</td><td>Lake</td><td>Nia</td><td>U17</td><td>Football</td><td>140</td></tr><tr><td>Ms.</td><td>Lisa</td><td>Brooks</td><td>Tyrese</td><td>U15</td><td>Football</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>Mr.</td><td>Omar</td><td>Peterson</td><td>Kayla</td><td>U17</td><td>Basketball</td><td>0</td></tr></table>","tasks":["Create the data source above in Excel (or Type a New List).","Write a welcome letter using Greeting Line and the fields CamperName, AgeGroup and Sport.","Add an If…Then…Else rule: if Balance > 0 show “Please pay your balance of $«Balance» by 30 June”, else “Thank you, your fees are fully paid”.","Filter to Sport Equal to Football, sort by ParentLastName, preview, and merge to a new document.","Create name-badge labels for all campers with Update Labels.","Build a registration form with a Plain Text name, a Date Picker for date of birth, a Drop-Down List for age group, and Check Boxes for allergies; protect it for Filling in forms and save as a template (.dotx).","Write a three-page camp handbook with Heading 1/2 styles and generate a TOC; add a new heading and update the entire table."],"skills":["Mail merge","Rules","Filtering and sorting","Labels","Content controls","Restrict Editing","Templates","Table of contents"],"check":[{"c":"Data source correct","m":2},{"c":"Fields and greeting correct","m":2},{"c":"Rule works for paid and unpaid","m":3},{"c":"Filter and sort applied (3 letters)","m":2},{"c":"Labels produced","m":2},{"c":"Form controls and protection","m":3},{"c":"TOC generated and updated","m":2}],"tip":"The filter should leave exactly three football families: Hodge, Lake and Brooks. If you get a different number, check spelling consistency in the Sport column."},{"id":"S4-L3","sec":"S4","units":["S4U4","S4U5"],"app":"web","level":"Core","title":"Build the Eco Club website","time":90,"brief":"<p>Plan and build a three-page website for <b>Frigate Bay Eco Club</b> using the Web Page Builder, an online builder or HTML.</p>","data":"<h4>Club facts</h4><ul><li>Purpose: recruit volunteers and report clean-up results.</li><li>Audience: students 12–18 (mostly on phones) and parents.</li><li>Clean-ups: first Saturday of each month, 7 a.m., meet at the boardwalk.</li><li>Results: Jan 42 kg, Feb 37 kg, Mar 51 kg.</li><li>E-mail: info@frigatebayeco.example.kn</li><li>Files: clean-up-rota.pdf, logo.png, cleanup.jpg</li></ul>","tasks":["Draw a site map (Home, Clean-ups, Contact) and a wireframe for each page.","Create a consistent template: logo in the header, navigation bar, content area and footer with “last updated”.","Home: welcome heading, short paragraph, compressed photo with meaningful alt text.","Clean-ups: a results table with a header row and a bookmark link “Jump to results”.","Contact: an e-mail link and a link to download clean-up-rota.pdf.","Check the pages three ways: preview, in a local browser, and after publishing.","Record a test log of at least six tests (each link type, a phone view, and a keyboard-only check)."],"skills":["Site map","Wireframe","Templates","Alt text","HTML tables","Four hyperlink types","Testing"],"check":[{"c":"Site map and wireframes","m":2},{"c":"Consistent template on all pages","m":3},{"c":"Image optimised with alt text","m":2},{"c":"Table correct","m":2},{"c":"All four link types work","m":4},{"c":"Test log complete","m":2}],"tip":"Name every file in lowercase with no spaces (clean-up-rota.pdf, not Clean Up Rota.PDF) and keep images in an images folder: most broken links come from file names."},{"id":"S4-L4","sec":"S4","units":["S4U5"],"app":"web","level":"Challenge","title":"Paper 032 style: fix and evaluate the ferry site","time":90,"brief":"<p>You are given <b>BGI Island Ferry Express</b> website files, which contain deliberate errors. Find and fix them, then write an evaluation, as in a Paper 032 practical question.</p>","data":"<h4>Known symptoms</h4><ul><li>The “Book by e-mail” link does nothing.</li><li>“Jump to fares” on timetable.html does not move.</li><li>The PDF fare list gives 404 after upload.</li><li>The home page takes over 20 seconds to load on a phone.</li><li>The timetable is an image of a printed sheet dated last season.</li><li>Gallery images have no alt text.</li></ul>","tasks":["Diagnose and fix each broken link (check mailto:, bookmark ids and case, file paths and uploads).","Replace the image timetable with an up-to-date HTML table showing a “last updated” date.","Resize and compress the home page photo and convert the gallery to thumbnails linking to full-size images.","Add meaningful alt text to every image and check colour contrast.","Retest on a phone and a laptop, in two browsers, recording before/after results.","Write a 400-word evaluation against accuracy, usability, display on devices, accessibility and load time, ending with an overall judgement.","Time limit: complete tasks 1–5 in 60 minutes, as in an examination."],"skills":["Debugging links","HTML tables","Image optimisation","Thumbnails","Accessibility","Testing","Evaluation"],"check":[{"c":"Three link faults fixed","m":3},{"c":"Accurate HTML timetable","m":2},{"c":"Load time improved with evidence","m":2},{"c":"Alt text and contrast","m":2},{"c":"Before/after test log","m":2},{"c":"Evaluation with judgement","m":4}],"tip":"Fix accuracy and broken core links first: a wrong ferry time does more harm than a slow photo. Prioritise by impact on the site's purpose."},{"id":"S5-L1","sec":"S5","units":["S5U1","S5U2","S5U3"],"app":"excel","level":"Foundation","title":"Employee payroll: formulas","time":60,"brief":"<p>A company needs its payroll calculated. Create the worksheet below named <b>Employees</b> and calculate Gross Pay, Medical, Tax and Net Pay with formulas.</p>","data":"<h4>Employees</h4><table><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th><th>D</th><th>E</th><th>F</th><th>G</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Employee</td><td>Salary</td><td>Allowance</td><td>Gross Pay</td><td>Medical</td><td>Tax</td><td>Net Pay</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Lawrence</td><td>980000</td><td>40000</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Karen</td><td>45000</td><td>9000</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Seeram</td><td>750000</td><td>35000</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Khemraj</td><td>40000</td><td>8000</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Mohan</td><td>54000</td><td>8000</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table><p>Gross Pay = Salary + Allowance · Medical is 5% of Salary · Tax is 33% of (Gross Pay − 35000) · Net Pay = Gross Pay − (Medical + Tax)</p>","tasks":["Create the worksheet named Employees with a light fill colour on the column headings.","Enter the formulas for Gross Pay, Medical, Tax and Net Pay in row 2 and copy them down to row 6.","Right-align the headings for the numeric data and place all borders in cells A1 to G6.","Insert a row above A1 and type the title 'Employees Salaries': bold, Arial, size 16, centred across A1 to G1 (Merge & Center).","Format the page to landscape orientation, centre the sheet horizontally and vertically, and format all values as currency.","Insert a new sheet, copy the Employees data to it, display the formulas, adjust the columns and rename the sheet Formulas.","Save as SALARIES in the Spreadsheet folder within the Class Files folder on your pen drive."],"skills":["Formulas with brackets and %","Replication with the fill handle","Borders, fill and alignment","Merge & Center","Page setup","Show Formulas","Renaming sheets"],"check":[{"c":"Gross Pay, Medical, Tax and Net Pay formulas correct and replicated","m":8},{"c":"Formatting (fill, alignment, borders, title)","m":5},{"c":"Page setup and currency","m":3},{"c":"Formulas sheet","m":2},{"c":"Saved correctly","m":2}],"tip":"Karen's row is a good check: Gross Pay 54000, Medical 2250, Tax 6270, Net Pay 45480. If your tax is 42450, you forgot the brackets."},{"id":"S5-L2","sec":"S5","units":["S5U2"],"app":"excel","level":"Foundation","title":"Student marks: functions and IF","time":45,"brief":"<p>Create the worksheet below named <b>Students</b> and use functions to analyse the marks.</p>","data":"<h4>Students</h4><table><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Students</td><td>Marks</td><td>Status</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Mohan</td><td>65</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Khemraj</td><td>72</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Triko</td><td>45</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Adrial</td><td>35</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Jones</td><td>40</td><td></td></tr></table>","tasks":["Create the worksheet named Students and insert the date in cell D1 (=TODAY()).","Centre the spreadsheet horizontally and vertically on the page.","Calculate the Status: a student is given \"PASS\" if the mark is over 60, else \"FAIL\" (=IF(B2>60,\"PASS\",\"FAIL\")).","In A8 to A11 type the labels Highest Mark, Lowest Mark, Average Mark and Number of Students.","In B8 to B11 calculate them with MAX, MIN, AVERAGE and COUNT.","Place all borders around A1 to D6 and an outside border around A8 to B11.","Insert a new sheet, copy the Students data, display the formulas, adjust the columns and rename the sheet Formulas.","Save as FUNCTIONS in the Spreadsheet folder within the Class Files folder on your pen drive."],"skills":["TODAY()","IF with text results","MAX, MIN, AVERAGE, COUNT","Borders","Show Formulas"],"check":[{"c":"IF formula correct and copied","m":4},{"c":"Summary functions correct","m":4},{"c":"Date, borders and centring","m":3},{"c":"Formulas sheet and saving","m":3}],"tip":"Expected: Highest 72, Lowest 35, Average 51.4, Number of Students 5; only Mohan and Khemraj PASS."},{"id":"S5-L3","sec":"S5","units":["S5U4"],"app":"excel","level":"Core","title":"Sorting and filtering","time":60,"brief":"<p>Two classic data tasks. Part A sorts the IT Centre staff list; Part B filters an Employees list.</p>","data":"<h4>Part A: Staff</h4><table><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>IT CENTRE</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Staff</td><td>Position</td><td>Salary (US$)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Khemraj</td><td>Network Engineer</td><td>950</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Adrial</td><td>Technician</td><td>400</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Yogesh</td><td>Technician</td><td>250</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Mohan</td><td>Network Engineer</td><td>750</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Ramnarine</td><td>Technician</td><td>325</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Ron</td><td>Technician</td><td>350</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Gregory</td><td>Network Engineer</td><td>800</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Paul</td><td>Network Engineer</td><td>850</td></tr></table><h4>Part B: Employees</h4><table><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th><th>D</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Employees</td><td>Gender</td><td>Salary</td><td>Age</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Alvin</td><td>Male</td><td>6500</td><td>25</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Miriam</td><td>Female</td><td>5300</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Pedro</td><td>Male</td><td>5200</td><td>31</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Tracy</td><td>Female</td><td>6500</td><td>19</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Spencer</td><td>Male</td><td>8000</td><td>28</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Suzie</td><td>Female</td><td>4500</td><td>22</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Ricky</td><td>Male</td><td>4500</td><td>28</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Trevor</td><td>Male</td><td>5500</td><td>32</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Melissa</td><td>Female</td><td>7500</td><td>35</td></tr></table>","tasks":["Part A: type the Staff worksheet with all borders and a fill colour on the title and headings. Insert the date and time (=NOW()) in D2 and Merge & Center the title across A1 to D1.","Right-align the Salary heading and format salaries as currency with two decimal places.","Copy the data to a new sheet, sort on the Staff column in ascending order and rename the sheet 'Sorting 1'.","Copy the data to another new sheet; sort with Position as the primary sort field (descending) and Salary as the secondary sort field (ascending). Rename it 'Sorting 2'. Save as SORTING.","Part B: type the Employees worksheet with all borders and a light fill on the headings; right-align the Salary and Age headings; format salaries as currency with zero decimal places; centre the sheet on the page.","Copy the data to a new sheet and filter for Male employees over 25 years who earn more than 5000. Rename the sheet 'Filter 1'.","Copy the data to another new sheet and find all Female employees who earn less than 6000. Rename it 'Filter 2'. Save as FILTERING."],"skills":["Custom Sort with Add Level","Ascending and descending","AutoFilter: text and number filters","Copying sheets","Currency formatting"],"check":[{"c":"Sorting 1 correct","m":2},{"c":"Sorting 2 correct (primary and secondary)","m":4},{"c":"Filter 1 correct","m":3},{"c":"Filter 2 correct","m":3},{"c":"Formatting and saving","m":3}],"tip":"Check Sorting 2: Technicians first (Yogesh, Ramnarine, Ron, Adrial), then Network Engineers (Mohan, Gregory, Paul, Khemraj). Filter 1 shows Pedro, Spencer and Trevor; Filter 2 shows Miriam and Suzie."},{"id":"S5-L4","sec":"S5","units":["S5U3","S5U5"],"app":"excel","level":"Core","title":"Linking worksheets and absolute addressing","time":75,"brief":"<p>Part A links a loan sheet to an interest-rate sheet. Part B is the Superior Car Company sales report.</p>","data":"<h4>Part A: Interest Rate sheet</h4><table><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Loans Interest Rate</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Interest Rate:</td><td>9.5%</td></tr></table><h4>Part A: Loans sheet</h4><table><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Loans and Interest</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Types of Loans</td><td>Loan Amounts</td><td>Interest Amounts</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Land</td><td>35000</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>House</td><td>280000</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Personal</td><td>18000</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Education</td><td>90000</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Business</td><td>150000</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Vehicle</td><td>75000</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Totals</td><td></td><td></td></tr></table><h4>Part B: Info sheet</h4><table><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Gov&#x27;t Tax:</td><td>20%</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>License Fee:</td><td>$500.00</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Insurance:</td><td>5%</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Model</td><td>Qty.</td><td>Showroom Price</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Audi e-Tron</td><td>5</td><td>25000</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Jaguar I-Pace</td><td>7</td><td>20500</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Volvo XC40</td><td>4</td><td>45000</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Ford Eco-Sport</td><td>9</td><td>17850</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>BMW X2</td><td>3</td><td>50400</td></tr></table><p>Columns D to I: Gov't Tax, Insurance Premium, License Fee, Total Value (price on the road), Monthly Sales, Sales Status.</p>","tasks":["Part A: type the Interest Rate sheet with Merge & Center, gridlines and a light fill, title and label in bold.","Create the Loans sheet; calculate the Interest Amounts with a link and an absolute reference: =B3*'Interest Rate'!$B$3, copied down.","Calculate totals for both columns (dark blue, bold, italic); format money as Currency with two decimals; wrap and right-align the value headings; centre the title (size 14, red).","Add a header with your name (right, bold, italic) and a footer with your address (centred, bold); centre both sheets on the page; add a Formulas sheet. Save as LINKING WORKSHEETS.","Part B: calculate Gov't Tax, Insurance Premium and License Fee with ABSOLUTE references to B1, B3 and B2, and Total Value and Monthly Sales with RELATIVE references. Rename the sheet Info.","Insert the date in E1; total all value columns except Showroom Price; format money as Currency with zero decimals.","Add Sales Status with =IF(H5>200000,\"High\",\"Low\").","In A12:A15 add Average Total Value, Maximum Monthly Sales, Minimum Government Tax and Number of Vehicles, and calculate them in B12:B15 with functions; add an outside border.","Insert three rows above A1 for the title 'Superior Car Company Sales' (Arial 20, red) and subtitle 'For the Month of June' (Times New Roman 16, dark blue, italic), centred across A1:I1. Landscape, centred.","Sort by Monthly Sales descending; add a Formulas sheet; a Filter sheet showing models beginning with V; and a column chart sheet named COLUMN titled 'Car Sales for June'. Save as ABSOLUTE ADDRESSING."],"skills":["Linking with SheetName!Cell","Absolute and relative references","IF","Headers and footers","Text filter Begins With","Column chart"],"check":[{"c":"Linked interest formulas","m":4},{"c":"Absolute/relative formulas in Info","m":6},{"c":"IF and summary functions","m":4},{"c":"Formatting, header/footer, page setup","m":4},{"c":"Sort, filter and chart","m":4},{"c":"Formulas sheets and saving","m":2}],"tip":"Interest total should be $61,560.00. Volvo XC40: Total Value $56,750, Monthly Sales $227,000 (High). After inserting the three title rows, check that the rate references updated to $B$4, $B$5 and $B$6."},{"id":"S5-L5","sec":"S5","units":["S5U5"],"app":"excel","level":"Challenge","title":"Charts and the COLLEGE workbook","time":90,"brief":"<p>Part A charts IPv6 address data (class exercise figures). Part B builds a two-sheet COLLEGE workbook with linking, functions, sorting, filtering and charts.</p>","data":"<h4>Part A: IPv6 data</h4><table><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Country</td><td>Country Code</td><td>IPv6 Addresses</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Germany</td><td>GE</td><td>9500</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Japan</td><td>JP</td><td>8300</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Australia</td><td>AU</td><td>8200</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>United Kingdom</td><td>UK</td><td>1200</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>United States of America</td><td>US</td><td>1100</td></tr></table><h4>Part B: Student sheet</h4><table><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th><th>D</th><th>E</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Surname</td><td>First name</td><td>Gender</td><td>Department</td><td>Credits</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Smith</td><td>Marvin</td><td>M</td><td>Computer Science</td><td>32</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Jackson</td><td>Alvin</td><td>M</td><td>Mathematics</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Martin</td><td>Melissa</td><td>F</td><td>History</td><td>28</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Archibald</td><td>Mavis</td><td>F</td><td>Sociology</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Williams</td><td>Mickey</td><td>M</td><td>Chemistry</td><td>30</td></tr></table>","tasks":["Part A: wrap the column headings, add a light fill, right-align C1, add borders and centre the sheet on the page.","Create a pie chart on a new sheet named PIE titled 'IPv6 Addresses for Each Country', with data labels showing value and percentage and a legend; title bold 20 pt, labels and legend bold 14 pt.","Create a bar chart (sheet BAR), a column chart (sheet COLUMN) and a line chart (sheet LINE) with the same title, data labels and axis titles. Then write two sentences on which chart type suits this data best and why the line chart does not. Save as IPV6ADDRESSES.","Part B: create COLLEGE with sheets 'Student' and 'Fees'. Add the title \"Students' Credits\" (bold, Arial 18) centred across A1:E1; middle-align and fill the headings; wrap 'First name'; landscape, centred.","On Fees, use link formulas to bring in Surname, First name and Credits (no Gender or Department). Add Tuition = Credits * 4000, Currency with zero decimals.","In A9:A12 enter Total Tuition:, Maximum Credits:, Minimum Tuition:, Average Credit: and calculate them in B9:B12 with functions; outside border.","Sort the Fees data by Tuition descending; add a Formulas sheet; add a Filter sheet showing students with Tuition greater than 100,000.","Create a pie chart (sheet PIE) of Students and Credits titled \"Students' Credits\" with data labels and percentages, and a bar chart (sheet BAR) of Students and Tuition titled \"Students' Tuition\" with data labels and axis titles. Resave."],"skills":["Chart types and chart sheets","Chart elements and formatting","Linking sheets","Functions","Sort and filter on copies"],"check":[{"c":"Four IPv6 charts correctly built and labelled","m":6},{"c":"Written chart evaluation","m":2},{"c":"Linked Fees sheet and Tuition","m":4},{"c":"Summary functions","m":4},{"c":"Sort, filter and Formulas sheet","m":3},{"c":"COLLEGE charts","m":4}],"tip":"Total Tuition $536,000; Maximum Credits 32; Minimum Tuition $80,000; Average Credit 26.8. The filter shows Smith, Williams and Martin."},{"id":"S5-L6","sec":"S5","units":["S5U2","S5U4"],"app":"excel","level":"Challenge","title":"Pivot tables and VLOOKUP","time":60,"brief":"<p>Part A summarises the SALARIES payroll with a pivot table. Part B uses VLOOKUP with a named range to find which attendees paid for a function.</p>","data":"<h4>Part B: Function payments</h4><table><tr><th></th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th><th>D</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Persons Who Attended a Function and Paid</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Received Payment</td><td>Amount Paid</td><td>Attended</td><td>Paid</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Albert</td><td>$99.00</td><td>Mary</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Allan</td><td>$25.00</td><td>Joe</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Ann</td><td>$125.00</td><td>James</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Bill</td><td>$85.00</td><td>Mike</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Charles</td><td>$201.00</td><td>Tina</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>James</td><td>$88.00</td><td>Judy</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Joe</td><td>$99.00</td><td>Allan</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Judy</td><td>$75.00</td><td>Chris</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Mary</td><td>$125.00</td><td>Tony</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Paul</td><td>$85.00</td><td>Bill</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Peter</td><td>$101.00</td><td>Becky</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>Steve</td><td>$88.00</td><td>Suzy</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>Suzy</td><td>$99.00</td><td>Jackie</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>Tina</td><td>$88.00</td><td>Donald</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>Tony</td><td>$99.00</td><td>Albert</td><td></td></tr></table>","tasks":["Part A: open SALARIES (Lab S5-L1). Create a pivot table on a new sheet summarising the totals of Salary, Allowance, Gross Pay, Medical, Tax and Net Pay for each Employee.","Rename the 'Row Labels' heading as Employees; add a title; format to landscape and centre on the page; rename the sheet Pivot Table; resave.","Part B: type the worksheet. Select A3:B17, right-click, Define Name, type PAID, OK.","Click D3, Insert Function, VLOOKUP: Lookup_value C3, Table_array PAID, Col_index_num 1, Range_lookup FALSE; press Enter.","Fill down from D3 to D17. Names that do not match display #N/A.","Below the table, write which attendees did not pay and explain why FALSE was essential.","Save as VLOOKUP FUNCTION."],"skills":["Insert ▸ PivotTable","Values area and renaming headings","Define Name","VLOOKUP with exact match","Interpreting #N/A"],"check":[{"c":"Pivot table summarises all six columns per employee","m":5},{"c":"Pivot formatting and sheet name","m":3},{"c":"Named range PAID","m":2},{"c":"VLOOKUP correct and filled down","m":4},{"c":"Explanation of #N/A and FALSE","m":3}],"tip":"Five attendees show #N/A: Mike, Chris, Becky, Jackie and Donald. With TRUE instead of FALSE, Mike would wrongly show Mary."},{"id":"S6-L1","sec":"S6","units":["S6U1","S6U2"],"app":"access","level":"Foundation","title":"The Storms database: build, edit and modify","time":50,"brief":"<p>You are a weather officer recording the 2008 hurricane season (practice data). Create the database, enter the storms, correct an error and change the structure.</p>","data":"<h4>Table structure: Hurricanes</h4><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Field name</th><th>Data type</th><th>Field size</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>StormName</td><td>Text</td><td></td><td>Name of the storm</td></tr><tr><td>Origin</td><td>Text</td><td></td><td>Place of origin of storm</td></tr><tr><td>Date of origin</td><td>Date/Time</td><td></td><td>Date storm was formed</td></tr><tr><td>Category</td><td>Number</td><td>Long Integer</td><td>Category of storm (1 to 5)</td></tr><tr><td>Major hurricane</td><td>Yes/No</td><td></td><td>Whether the storm became a major hurricane or not</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h4>Records to enter</h4><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>StormName</th><th>Origin</th><th>Date of origin</th><th>Category</th><th>Major hurricane</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bertha</td><td>Coast of Africa</td><td>03/07/2008</td><td>3</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Dolly</td><td>Caribbean Sea</td><td>20/07/2008</td><td>2</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Gustav</td><td>Windward Islands</td><td>25/08/2008</td><td>4</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Hanna</td><td>Leeward Islands</td><td>28/08/2008</td><td>2</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Kyle</td><td>Caribbean Sea</td><td>29/09/2008</td><td>2</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h4>Fatality values</h4><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>StormName</th><th>Fatality</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bertha</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Dolly</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Gustav</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Hanna</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Kyle</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tasks":["Open Access, choose Blank desktop database and name it Storms.","Close the default Table1, then Create ▸ Table Design.","Enter the five fields with the data types, the Long Integer field size for Category and the descriptions shown.","Set an appropriate primary key (StormName for this one season) and save the table as Hurricanes.","Switch to Datasheet View and enter the five records.","Change Kyle's category from 2 to 1.","In Design View add Fatality (Yes/No) as the last field; enter the Fatality values.","Add the description \"Whether storm led to deaths\" to Fatality and add the validation rule Between 1 And 5 to Category with suitable validation text.","Sort the datasheet by Date of origin, oldest first, and take a screenshot."],"skills":["Create a database and table in Design View","Choose data types and field sizes","Enter and edit records","Modify a table structure","Validation rule and text","Sort records"],"check":[{"c":"Correct field names, data types and size","m":3},{"c":"Five records entered accurately","m":2},{"c":"Kyle's category corrected","m":1},{"c":"Fatality field added with values and description","m":2},{"c":"Validation rule and text on Category","m":1},{"c":"Sorted by Date of origin","m":1}],"tip":"Save the design before switching to Datasheet View, and press Tab (not Enter) to move between columns in Design View."},{"id":"S6-L2","sec":"S6","units":["S6U2","S6U3","S6U4"],"app":"access","level":"Core","title":"Island Reads Library: relationships, queries and a form","time":75,"brief":"<p>Build the three-table Island Reads Library database, link it, then answer the librarian's questions with queries and create a member form with a loans subform.</p>","data":"<h4>tblBook</h4><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>BookID</th><th>Title</th><th>Genre</th><th>Price</th><th>YearPub</th><th>InStock</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>B001</td><td>Hurricane Season</td><td>Fiction</td><td>$24.50</td><td>2019</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>B002</td><td>Coding with Python</td><td>Computing</td><td>$45.00</td><td>2023</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>B003</td><td>Guavaberry Summer</td><td>Fiction</td><td>$18.75</td><td>2021</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>B004</td><td>Reefs of Rodney Bay</td><td>Science</td><td>$32.00</td><td>2018</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>B005</td><td>The Sulphur Springs Mystery</td><td>Mystery</td><td>$15.00</td><td>2022</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>B006</td><td>Cricket Legends of the West Indies</td><td>Sport</td><td>$28.00</td><td>2015</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>B007</td><td>Front Street Stories</td><td>Fiction</td><td>$21.00</td><td>2020</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>B008</td><td>Databases Made Simple</td><td>Computing</td><td>$39.99</td><td>2024</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>B009</td><td>Mysteries of the Pitons</td><td>Mystery</td><td>$19.50</td><td>2017</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>B010</td><td>Steelpan Rhythms</td><td>Music</td><td>$26.00</td><td>2021</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>B011</td><td>Sargassum and the Sea</td><td>Science</td><td>$35.50</td><td>2023</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>B012</td><td>Silk Cotton Folk Tales</td><td>Fiction</td><td>$12.00</td><td>2016</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h4>tblMember (MemberID is AutoNumber)</h4><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>MemberID</th><th>FirstName</th><th>LastName</th><th>District</th><th>MemberType</th><th>DateJoined</th><th>Phone</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Kayla</td><td>Richardson</td><td>Gros Islet</td><td>Student</td><td>14/09/2024</td><td>542-1187</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Jaden</td><td>Fleming</td><td>Castries</td><td>Student</td><td>20/01/2025</td><td>542-3360</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Marisol</td><td>Baptiste</td><td>Rodney Bay</td><td>Adult</td><td>02/05/2023</td><td>544-0912</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Tyrese</td><td>Hodge</td><td>Soufrière</td><td>Student</td><td>11/03/2025</td><td>543-7781</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Gloria</td><td>Auguste</td><td>Castries</td><td>Senior</td><td>30/11/2022</td><td>542-5504</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Nathan</td><td>Lake</td><td>Babonneau</td><td>Adult</td><td>17/02/2024</td><td>543-2219</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Amara</td><td>Connor</td><td>Bexon</td><td>Student</td><td>05/09/2025</td><td>544-8873</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Desmond</td><td>Carty</td><td>Gros Islet</td><td>Senior</td><td>19/08/2023</td><td>542-9046</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h4>tblLoan</h4><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>LoanID</th><th>MemberID</th><th>BookID</th><th>DateOut</th><th>DateDue</th><th>Returned</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>L001</td><td>1</td><td>B003</td><td>01/09/2026</td><td>15/09/2026</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>L002</td><td>1</td><td>B005</td><td>20/09/2026</td><td>04/10/2026</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>L003</td><td>2</td><td>B002</td><td>22/09/2026</td><td>06/10/2026</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>L004</td><td>3</td><td>B004</td><td>25/09/2026</td><td>09/10/2026</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>L005</td><td>4</td><td>B001</td><td>01/10/2026</td><td>15/10/2026</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>L006</td><td>5</td><td>B012</td><td>02/10/2026</td><td>16/10/2026</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>L007</td><td>2</td><td>B008</td><td>05/10/2026</td><td>19/10/2026</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>L008</td><td>6</td><td>B006</td><td>07/10/2026</td><td>21/10/2026</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>L009</td><td>7</td><td>B007</td><td>10/10/2026</td><td>24/10/2026</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>L010</td><td>3</td><td>B011</td><td>12/10/2026</td><td>26/10/2026</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tasks":["Create the three tables in Design View with suitable data types (MemberID AutoNumber in tblMember, Number (Long Integer) in tblLoan) and set primary keys.","Add input mask 000\\-0000 to Phone and validation rule >=0 (with text) to Price.","Enter the records.","Create relationships tblMember → tblLoan and tblBook → tblLoan with referential integrity enforced.","qryFictionUnder20: Fiction books under $20 (expect 2).","qryOverdue: FirstName, LastName, Title for loans with DateDue <#2026-10-20# and Returned No (expect 4 rows).","qrySale: Title, Price and SalePrice: [Price]*0.9 formatted as Currency.","Use the Form Wizard to build frmMember with a loans subform (Datasheet layout)."],"skills":["Primary and foreign keys","Input masks and validation","Relationships and referential integrity","AND criteria","Multi-table query","Calculated field","Form with subform"],"check":[{"c":"Tables, types and keys correct","m":3},{"c":"Mask and validation work","m":2},{"c":"Relationships with 1 and ∞ shown","m":2},{"c":"qryFictionUnder20 returns 2 books","m":1},{"c":"qryOverdue returns 4 rows","m":2},{"c":"SalePrice correct","m":2},{"c":"Form with working subform","m":2}],"tip":"If the Form Wizard does not offer \"Form with subform(s)\", the relationship is missing. If a query returns 96 rows, tblLoan has not been added to join the tables."},{"id":"S6-L3","sec":"S6","units":["S6U2","S6U3","S6U4"],"app":"access","level":"Challenge","title":"SBA rehearsal: San Pedro Car Rentals","time":120,"brief":"<p>A full SBA-style database task under the CSEC limits: at most three tables, two queries, one calculation, one form with a subform and one grouped, sorted report.</p>","data":"<h4>CUSTOMER</h4><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>CustomerID</th><th>FirstName</th><th>LastName</th><th>Phone</th><th>LicenceNo</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Shanice</td><td>Benjamin</td><td>543-2219</td><td>ANU10442</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Rohan</td><td>Persaud</td><td>542-7781</td><td>ANU20918</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Gloria</td><td>Samuel</td><td>544-0912</td><td>ANU11587</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Tevin</td><td>Brooks</td><td>543-4410</td><td>ANU30021</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Maya</td><td>Hodge</td><td>542-3360</td><td>ANU28870</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Desmond</td><td>Carty</td><td>542-9046</td><td>ANU17733</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h4>CAR</h4><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>PlateNo</th><th>Make</th><th>Model</th><th>DailyRate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>PM-4410</td><td>Toyota</td><td>Yaris</td><td>$45.00</td></tr><tr><td>PM-2219</td><td>Kia</td><td>Rio</td><td>$38.00</td></tr><tr><td>PM-1187</td><td>Toyota</td><td>Corolla</td><td>$50.00</td></tr><tr><td>PM-7781</td><td>Hyundai</td><td>Tucson</td><td>$60.00</td></tr><tr><td>PM-5504</td><td>Kia</td><td>Picanto</td><td>$35.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h4>RENTAL</h4><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>RentalID</th><th>CustomerID</th><th>PlateNo</th><th>DateOut</th><th>Days</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>R101</td><td>1</td><td>PM-4410</td><td>02/09/2026</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>R102</td><td>2</td><td>PM-2219</td><td>03/09/2026</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>R103</td><td>3</td><td>PM-1187</td><td>05/09/2026</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>R104</td><td>4</td><td>PM-7781</td><td>08/09/2026</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>R105</td><td>2</td><td>PM-5504</td><td>12/09/2026</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>R106</td><td>5</td><td>PM-4410</td><td>14/09/2026</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>R107</td><td>1</td><td>PM-7781</td><td>18/09/2026</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>R108</td><td>6</td><td>PM-2219</td><td>20/09/2026</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>R109</td><td>3</td><td>PM-5504</td><td>23/09/2026</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>R110</td><td>4</td><td>PM-1187</td><td>27/09/2026</td><td>5</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tasks":["Create the three tables in Design View with appropriate field names, data types, sizes and primary keys; Days must have the validation rule Between 1 And 30.","Enter all records, then create relationships CUSTOMER → RENTAL and CAR → RENTAL with referential integrity.","Query 1 (one table, criteria): cars with DailyRate >40.","Query 2 (two or three tables, more than one criterion, one calculation): rentals in September 2026 (Between #2026-09-01# And #2026-09-30#) with Days >=3, showing LastName, Make, Days, DailyRate and Income: [Days]*[DailyRate].","Form Wizard: customer main form with a rentals subform.","Build a query of all rentals with Make and Income, then use the Report Wizard to group by Make, sort by DateOut, and show Sum and Count of Income per make and a grand total.","Give the report the title San Pedro Car Rentals: Rental Income by Car Make, September 2026 and save it as PDF.","Modify CUSTOMER by adding an Email field (Short Text, 60), and delete it again, taking before-and-after screenshots."],"skills":["Table design under SBA limits","Relationships","Criteria with dates and AND","Calculated field","Form with subform","Grouped report with summaries","Output to file","Modify structure"],"check":[{"c":"Tables, types, sizes and keys","m":4},{"c":"Relationships with integrity","m":2},{"c":"Query 1 returns PM-4410, PM-1187, PM-7781","m":2},{"c":"Query 2 criteria and Income correct","m":4},{"c":"Form with appropriate subform fields","m":2},{"c":"Report grouped and sorted with correct totals (Toyota $530.00, Kia $628.00, Hyundai $600.00; grand total $1,758.00)","m":4},{"c":"Specific title and PDF output","m":1},{"c":"Structure modification evidenced","m":1}],"tip":"Check your report totals by hand before you submit: a moderator who finds one wrong total doubts everything else."},{"id":"S7-L1","sec":"S7","units":["S7U1","S7U2"],"app":"diagram","level":"Foundation","title":"IPO tables and structure charts","time":50,"brief":"<p>Use Word tables and shapes (or draw.io) to analyse problems and design solutions top-down.</p>","data":"<h4>Problems</h4><table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Problem</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Accept three numbers and display their Sum.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Accept the radius of a circle and display its circumference (2 * 3.142 * Radius).</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Accept US dollars and display the EC dollar equivalent at 2.70.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Accept 25 test marks and display the average mark.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>A school library fines system (structure chart only).</td></tr></tbody></table>","tasks":["Create a 3-column table with headings Input, Processing, Output for problems 1–4.","Fill the Processing column using the pattern Accept / Calculate X (formula) / Store results in X / Display X.","Shade the Input column light blue and the Output column light yellow.","Using SmartArt hierarchy or shapes, draw a structure chart for problem 5 with a top module, at least three level 1 modules and two level 2 modules.","Add your name and form class in the header and save as S7_L1_YourName.docx."],"skills":["Analysing problems with IPO tables","Using Word tables and shading","Drawing structure charts"],"check":[{"c":"Four correct IPO tables","m":8},{"c":"Processing in Accept/Calculate/Store/Display order","m":4},{"c":"Structure chart with three levels","m":4},{"c":"Formatting and file naming","m":2}],"tip":"Inputs and outputs are data items (nouns); actions (verbs) belong in Processing."},{"id":"S7-L2","sec":"S7","units":["S7U3","S7U4","S7U5"],"app":"code","level":"Core","title":"From pseudocode to trace table to Pascal","time":80,"brief":"<p>Take three class algorithms through the full pipeline: pseudocode, flowchart, trace table and a working Pascal program.</p>","data":"<h4>Algorithms</h4><p>A. Caribe Shop 15% discount (sequence). B. Exam grades E/G/S/US/VUS (nested IF). C. Total of numbers until 0 is entered (WHILE loop).</p><pre>Start\n  Write \"Enter customer name and gallons used: \"\n  Read Name, Gallons\n  IF Gallons &gt;= 1000 THEN\n    Charge ← 100 + Gallons * 0.05\n  ELSE IF Gallons &gt;= 500 THEN\n    Charge ← 50 + Gallons * 0.03\n  ELSE\n    Charge ← 50 + Gallons * 0.02\n  ENDIF\n  Write Name, \"owes $\", Charge\nStop</pre><p>Extension: the water company bill above.</p>","tasks":["Write the pseudocode for A, B and C in the class style (Start, Write prompt, Read, ←, IF … ENDIF, WHILE … ENDWHILE, Stop).","Draw the flowchart for B using correct symbols.","Choose normal, boundary and erroneous test data for B and C, with expected results.","Desk check B and C with trace tables.","Type and run A, B and C in Pascal (Uses Crt, Var, Begin, Clrscr, ReadLn, WriteLn with :8:2, End.).","Record actual outputs next to your expected results; fix any differences."],"skills":["Writing pseudocode","Drawing flowcharts","Trace tables and test data","Coding in Pascal"],"check":[{"c":"Three correct pseudocode algorithms","m":6},{"c":"Correct flowchart for B","m":4},{"c":"Test plans with all three data types","m":4},{"c":"Accurate trace tables","m":4},{"c":"Three working Pascal programs","m":6}],"tip":"Test 80, 79, 60, 59, 45, 44, 33 and 32 for the grades algorithm: every boundary."},{"id":"S7-L3","sec":"S7","units":["S7U6"],"app":"code","level":"Challenge","title":"Robo Lab: from blocks to Pascal","time":90,"brief":"<p>Solve three Robo Lab missions of increasing difficulty, then convert your blocks into pseudocode, a flowchart and Pascal.</p>","data":"<h4>Missions</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Mission</th><th>Concepts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Park patrol: drive the square edge and return</td><td>Repeat loop</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Beach clean-up: count bottles over 10 squares</td><td>Sensor, IF, counter variable</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Warehouse maze: reach the exit with the right-hand rule</td><td>Repeat until, nested IF-ELSE</td></tr></tbody></table>","tasks":["Solve each mission in Robo Lab and screenshot the blocks.","Copy Robo Lab's pseudocode for each and check it line by line against your blocks.","Hand-draw (or draw.io) the flowchart for the maze mission.","Write the Pascal version of the beach clean-up, assuming Robo Lab provides DriveForward, BottleSeen and PickUp.","Create a custom block for one repeated routine and explain how it maps to a Pascal procedure.","Write a short evaluation: when does the right-hand rule fail, and what would you change?"],"skills":["Block-based programming","Sensors and decisions","Converting between representations","Procedures and custom blocks"],"check":[{"c":"Three missions solved","m":6},{"c":"Accurate pseudocode","m":4},{"c":"Correct maze flowchart","m":4},{"c":"Correct Pascal translation","m":4},{"c":"Custom block explained","m":3},{"c":"Evaluation","m":3}],"tip":"Scratch's [repeat until] tests first: translate it as WHILE NOT … DO, not REPEAT … UNTIL."},{"id":"S8-L1","sec":"S8","units":["S8U1","S8U3"],"app":"code","level":"Foundation","title":"From pseudocode to Pascal, Python and VBA: the Carnival ticket calculator","time":60,"brief":"<p>Your first full programs. You will turn a short algorithm into Pascal, Python and VBA, run each one and compare the syntax.</p>","data":"<h4>Ticket prices</h4><table><tr><th>Ticket</th><th>Price</th></tr><tr><td>Adult</td><td>$25</td></tr><tr><td>Child (under 12)</td><td>$10</td></tr></table><h4>Algorithm</h4><pre><code class=\"language-pseudocode\">Start\n   Write \"Adult tickets?\"\n   Read adults\n   Write \"Child tickets?\"\n   Read children\n   total ← adults * 25 + children * 10\n   IF total &gt; 100 THEN\n      Write \"Group discount applies\"\n   ENDIF\n   Write \"Total to pay: \", total\nStop</code></pre>","tasks":["Open Free Pascal or Lazarus. Type the program header, Uses Crt, Const ADULT_PRICE = 25 and CHILD_PRICE = 10, and a Var section declaring adults, children and total as Integer.","Translate each pseudocode line into Pascal (ReadLn, :=, If … Then, WriteLn). Compile; fix any syntax errors and write down each error message.","Run with 3 adults and 2 children (expected 95, no discount message) and 4 adults and 2 children (expected 120 with the discount message).","Write the same program in Python (IDLE or the Code Lab) using int(input()) and print().","In Excel: show the Developer tab, press Alt+F11, Insert ▸ Module, type Option Explicit and Sub CarnivalTickets(). Use Dim, InputBox and MsgBox. Run with F5 and save as .xlsm.","Complete a table comparing the three versions: assignment, input, output, IF syntax, comments."],"skills":["Declaring variables and constants","Input and output","Assignment and arithmetic","IF-THEN","Compiling and fixing syntax errors","Using the VBA editor"],"check":[{"c":"Pascal program compiles and gives correct results","m":3},{"c":"Python program runs correctly","m":2},{"c":"VBA macro runs in a saved .xlsm workbook","m":2},{"c":"Syntax comparison table complete and accurate","m":2},{"c":"Error messages recorded and explained","m":1}],"tip":"In Pascal, never put a semicolon directly before Else, and end the program with End. (full stop). In VBA, the workbook must be saved as .xlsm or the code disappears."},{"id":"S8-L2","sec":"S8","units":["S8U4"],"app":"code","level":"Core","title":"Loops and arrays: the hurricane-season rainfall logger","time":75,"brief":"<p>Use FOR, WHILE and REPEAT loops and a one-dimensional array to analyse rainfall data, in Pascal and in Excel VBA.</p>","data":"<h4>Rainfall readings, one week (mm)</h4><table><tr><th>Day</th><th>Mon</th><th>Tue</th><th>Wed</th><th>Thu</th><th>Fri</th><th>Sat</th><th>Sun</th></tr><tr><td>Rain</td><td>12.5</td><td>0</td><td>3.5</td><td>22</td><td>7.5</td><td>0.5</td><td>9</td></tr></table><p>Expected: total 55.0 mm, average 7.9 mm, wettest day 4 (Thu), driest 0.0 mm, rainy days 6.</p>","tasks":["Pascal: declare rain : Array[1..7] Of Real. Use a FOR loop to read the 7 readings into the array.","Add a REPEAT … UNTIL loop around each ReadLn so that only 0 to 500 is accepted.","Traverse the array to find the total, average (to 1 decimal place), wettest day (position) and number of rainy days (more than 0 mm).","Test with the data above and check your results against the expected values.","Excel: type the table into columns A and B (headings in row 1). Write a VBA Sub that reads Cells(r, 2) in a Do While loop until an empty cell, and writes the total into D2 and the average into D3.","Add an eighth day to the sheet and run the macro again: it should include the new day without changing the code."],"skills":["FOR, WHILE and REPEAT loops","Counters and accumulators","Arrays and traversal","Finding maximum and its position","Validation loops","VBA Cells and Range"],"check":[{"c":"Array declared and filled correctly","m":2},{"c":"Validation loop rejects -1 and 501","m":2},{"c":"Total, average, wettest day and rainy days correct","m":4},{"c":"VBA macro reads until an empty cell and writes results","m":3},{"c":"Works for 8 days without code changes","m":1}],"tip":"Initialise total to 0 BEFORE the loop, and start the wettest search with the first element, not with 0."},{"id":"S8-L3","sec":"S8","units":["S8U5","S8U6"],"app":"code","level":"Challenge","title":"SBA rehearsal: documented beach clean-up tracker in several languages","time":120,"brief":"<p>Produce an SBA-quality, fully documented program, then show the same algorithm in other languages.</p>","data":"<h4>Test data: bag weights (kg)</h4><table><tr><th>Test</th><th>Inputs</th><th>Expected output</th></tr><tr><td>1 Normal</td><td>12.5, 20, 9, 0</td><td>Bags: 3, Total: 41.5 kg, Keep going: 8.5 kg to go</td></tr><tr><td>2 Boundary</td><td>25, 25, 0</td><td>Bags: 2, Total: 50.0 kg, Target reached!</td></tr><tr><td>3 Boundary</td><td>0</td><td>Bags: 0, Total: 0.0 kg</td></tr><tr><td>4 Erroneous</td><td>-3, then 5, 0</td><td>-3 rejected; Bags: 1, Total: 5.0 kg</td></tr></table>","tasks":["Write the problem statement and an IPO chart.","Write the algorithm in pseudocode and draw the flowchart (WHILE loop with sentinel 0, validation of negative weights, IF for the 50 kg target).","Dry run tests 1 and 4 with a trace table.","Code it in Pascal with a program-head comment (purpose, author, dates, input, output), declaration comments, a ShowSummary procedure with a procedure head, and correct indentation.","Run all four tests; record expected and actual results with screenshots.","Translate the program into Python and VBA (and optionally JavaScript); run test 1 in each and confirm identical output.","Write a one-page user guide for volunteers."],"skills":["Problem definition","Algorithm design","Trace tables","Selection and iteration","Procedures","Internal and external documentation","Translation between languages"],"check":[{"c":"Design documents complete and consistent","m":3},{"c":"Trace table accurate","m":2},{"c":"Pascal program correct and fully documented","m":5},{"c":"All four tests recorded honestly","m":2},{"c":"Translations give identical results","m":2},{"c":"User guide clear and non-technical","m":2}],"tip":"Keep the variable names identical in your pseudocode, flowchart, trace table and code: moderators compare them line by line."},{"id":"S8-L4","sec":"S8","units":["S8U2"],"app":"code","level":"Core","title":"Bug hunt: syntax, logic and run-time errors","time":60,"brief":"<p>Find and fix every error in three faulty programs, classify each one, and prove the fixes with test data.</p>","data":"<h4>Faulty program 1 (Python)</h4><pre><code class=\"language-python\">price = 25\ntickets = int(input(\"How many tickets? \")\nif tickets &gt; 10\n    print(\"Group booking\")\nPrint(\"Total:\", price * tickets)</code></pre><h4>Faulty program 2 (Pascal)</h4><pre><code class=\"language-pascal\">Program Average_Bug;\nVar s1, s2, s3 : Integer; average : Real;\nBegin\n  ReadLn(s1); ReadLn(s2); ReadLn(s3);\n  average := s1 + s2 + s3 / 3;\n  WriteLn('Average: ', average:0:1);\nEnd.</code></pre><h4>Faulty program 3 (VBA)</h4><pre><code class=\"language-vba\">Sub ShareTips()\n    Dim tips As Integer, staff As Integer\n    tips = InputBox(\"Tips?\")\n    staff = InputBox(\"Staff?\")\n    MsgBox \"Each gets \" &amp; tips \\ staff\nEnd Sub</code></pre>","tasks":["Program 1: run it, record each syntax error message, fix them one at a time, and note which line the message pointed to.","Program 2: test with 30, 45, 60. Explain why the output is 95.0 instead of 45.0, classify the error and fix it.","Program 3: run it with 0 staff. Record the run-time error message, then add validation so staff must be at least 1.","Complete an error log table: program, line, error message (if any), error type, fix.","For program 2, write a test plan with normal, boundary and erroneous data."],"skills":["Reading error messages","Classifying errors","Debugging","Validation","Test planning"],"check":[{"c":"All syntax errors in program 1 fixed","m":3},{"c":"Logic error in program 2 explained and fixed","m":2},{"c":"Run-time error in program 3 recorded and prevented","m":2},{"c":"Error log complete and correct","m":2},{"c":"Test plan covers all three data types","m":1}],"tip":"Fix the FIRST error first, then translate again: one mistake can cause several messages further down."}]);
